    "body": "Closes #129.\n\nImplements ADR-016: inline elements now flow with surrounding text, the display property distinguishes block from inline, and the dir attribute controls text direction. The ADR-015 RTL heuristic divergence documented in current-state.md is resolved.\n\nSix commits, ~1500 lines added across the branch. Every feature visually verified with screenshots before commit.\n\n## What this fixes\n\n**Inline formatting.** Before this PR, `<p>Hello <em>world</em>!</p>` rendered as three vertically stacked blocks. Firefox renders it as one flowing line. That is the biggest structural gap remaining in the renderer -- real HTML uses inline elements constantly.\n\nAfter this PR: `<p>Hello <em>world</em>!</p>` renders as one flowing line, with inline element colors preserved. That is the ADR-016 payoff.\n\n**RTL heuristic divergence.** ADR-015 shipped a first-strong heuristic applied unconditionally: mixed-direction paragraphs rendered RTL even without an explicit dir attribute, diverging from Firefox. ADR-016 makes the heuristic opt-in via dir=\"auto\" and defaults to inherited direction (LTR at html). The welcome page's mixed-direction paragraph now renders left-aligned, matching Firefox.\n\n## Six commits\n\n**Commit 1** (`c4974b4`) -- display enum + inline node types\n- New Display enum { Block, Inline, None }\n- LayoutKind gains Inline and InlineContext\n- LayoutInline and LayoutInlineContext structs\n- LineFragment gains font_family, font_size, color fields\n- display_of() helper (defaults to Block when missing)\n\n**Commit 2** (`654c156`) -- inline context infrastructure\n- StyledWord and StyledLine types\n- break_styled_words_into_lines: greedy line breaking over styled words\n- paint.cpp handles all four LayoutKind values\n- LineDrawer signature simplified to (cairo_t*, LineFragment) -- fragments carry their own style\n\n**Commit 3** (`d787ac9`) -- inline flow (Block B)\n- flatten_inline_text helper\n- layout_element classifies children via display_of\n- flush_inline_run collapses whitespace across runs\n- 19 inline elements get display:inline in the UA stylesheet\n- 6 inline flow tests\n\n**Commit 4** (`a8a6334`) -- per-fragment style + RTL (Block C)\n- flatten_inline_to_words: emits styled words with per-element color\n- Two-path flush_inline_run: text-only uses LayoutText (ADR-015), inline-element runs use LayoutInlineContext (ADR-016)\n- RTL mirror formula preserves visual right-to-left order across fragments\n- 2 new tests (anchor color, RTL fragment reversal)\n- 5 Block B tests updated to walk LayoutInlineContext\n\n**Commit 5** (`e498d1f`) -- dir attribute (Block D)\n- New Direction enum { Ltr, Rtl }\n- resolve_direction: ltr -> Ltr, rtl -> Rtl, auto -> heuristic, missing -> inherit parent\n- layout_element threads parent_dir through recursion\n- detect_rtl calls in flush_inline_run replaced with own_dir check\n- 7 new [layout][direction] tests covering the four precedence cases\n- docs/current-state.md RTL section rewritten\n\n**Commit 6** (`912774c`) -- docs refresh\n- current-state.md: inline formatting, display, dir attribute, per-fragment style added to renders-correctly\n- README: feature matrix rows updated\n- decisions/README.md: ADR-016 added to index\n\n## Visual verification\n\nThree demonstration pages, all committed:\n\n**docs/inline-test.html** -- verified that:\n- `<p>Hello <em>world</em>!</p>` renders as one flowing line\n- `<p><em>a</em><em>b</em><em>c</em></p>` renders as \"abc\" (no inserted spaces)\n- `<p><em>a</em> <em>b</em></p>` renders as \"a b\" (space preserved)\n- Block children still interrupt inline runs cleanly\n\n**docs/inline-color-test.html** -- verified that:\n- `<a>` renders blue inside a flowing paragraph (UA stylesheet color reaches fragment)\n- `<span class=\"red\">` renders red, `<span class=\"blue\">` renders blue\n- Arabic RTL paragraph with inline element aligns correctly, colors preserved\n\n**docs/dir-test.html** -- verified all four direction cases:\n- No dir on English -> LEFT (inherit LTR)\n- dir=\"rtl\" on English -> RIGHT\n- dir=\"auto\" on Arabic -> RIGHT (heuristic opt-in)\n- Mixed paragraph with no dir -> LEFT (ADR-015 divergence resolved)\n\nWelcome page after Block D: 4th line (mixed Arabic+English) is now left-aligned. h1 orange 32px intact.\n\n## Known limitation (not a Block-XXX regression)\n\nInline `style=\"\"` attributes are NOT parsed into ComputedStyle. The cascade only sees stylesheet rules. `<span style=\"color: red\">` renders black. This is a pre-existing gap (never implemented; out of scope for ADR-009/010). Class-based and UA-stylesheet-provided colors work correctly. Deferred to a future inline-styles ADR.\n\n## Tests\n\n- 213 cases, 839 assertions, all pass (was 190/755 on main before this branch)\n- 8 inline flow tests\n- 7 direction tests\n- 2 paint tests for LayoutInlineContext\n- All existing 190 tests still pass\n\n## Deferred (per ADR-016)\n\n- display: none (retires the `<head>` skip list)\n- display: flex / grid / table\n- Baseline alignment (top-aligned in v1)\n- Inline boxes spanning block boundaries (fallback to block)\n- direction CSS property (only dir attribute in v1)\n- Full UAX #9 bidi reordering\n\n## Next\n\nWith ADR-016 landed, the natural next ADR is either:\n- display: none (small, retires the head skip list, unblocks `<head>` handling without a hardcoded list)\n- Pseudo-classes (:hover, :link, :visited)\n- At-rules (@media)\n\nEach its own ADR. This PR is the last major structural change before pages that use real-world CSS start looking like pages that use real-world CSS.\n",
